# THE BACKSTOP FOR A BYPASSED PRE-COMMIT.
#
# `pre-commit` is thorough and skippable, and it gets skipped for real reasons:
# lint-staged's fallow audit is scoped to the merge-base with master, so a branch
# that inherits a finding cannot commit until it pays down debt it did not
# create. `--no-verify` then skips oxlint and `oxfmt --write` as well, and those
# only ever saw the STAGED files anyway.
#
# That is how PR #218 pushed two unformatted files and learned about it from a
# red `oxfmt --check` minutes later. Push is the right moment for the whole-repo
# view: it catches every commit however it was made — bypassed hook, amend,
# rebase, squash — and it is the last point before the work leaves the machine.
#
# Everything here is a check CI also runs, and all of it together takes a couple
# of seconds. Keep it that way: the slow gates (coverage, the route smoke, the
# database suite) belong in CI and in a deliberate local run, not here, because
# a hook that costs minutes is a hook that gets bypassed too. `scripts/git-hooks.test.ts`
# pins both halves of that bargain.
#
# The env stripping is the same backstop as in pre-commit: git exports GIT_DIR &
# co. into its hooks, and any `git` a test spawns then targets THIS repository
# whatever its cwd.

bunx oxfmt --check
bunx oxlint

env -u GIT_DIR -u GIT_WORK_TREE -u GIT_INDEX_FILE -u GIT_PREFIX \
    -u GIT_COMMON_DIR -u GIT_OBJECT_DIRECTORY -u GIT_NAMESPACE \
    bun run test

bun run test:mocks
